 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? That's a natural effect of acrylic, it refracts and scatters light differently which makes it seem darker. You can use a lightbox or turn your studio around so the light comes from the side, not the window. Shoot a test image in morning and at evening, then compare them. Varnish helps, but it dulls the piece slightly. A wait few months first, the fresh finish is brighter than it stays.",
